hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1528","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of al-A’mash. H. Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, Abu Khaled told us. H Ali bin Khashram told us, Issa told us. H Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us. H. Salam bin Junada told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan. H Muhammad ibn Rafi’ told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar, and al-Thawri told us. H Abu Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Mu’ammal, Sufyan narrated to us, all of these, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The imam is guarantor, and the muezzin is trustworthy. O God, guide the imams and forgive the muezzins.” This is the hadith of Al-Ashjaj. Abu Bakr said: Ibn Numayr narrated it, on the authority of Al-Amash, but he corrupted the report."
"1529","Al-Ashjaj narrated, Ibn Numayr narrated, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I narrated on the authority of Abu Salih, and I do not think that I have heard him. He said: Abu Hurairah said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. It was narrated by Zuhayr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said something similar."
"1530","We are Musa bin Sahl Al-Ramli, we are Musa bin Daoud, we are Zuhayr bin Muawiyah. The news of Suhail was narrated by Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq and Muhammad bin Ammar, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and they did not mention al-A’mash in Attribution"
"1531","I am Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan, Yazid bin Zurayi told us, Abd Al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us. H Ali bin Hajar narrated to us, Muhammad bin Ammar narrated to us, both of them on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The muezzins are trustworthy, and the imams are trustworthy. O God, forgive the muezzins and protect the imams” three times, This is the wording of the hadith of Ali bin Hajar. Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan said: “May God guide the imams and forgive the muezzins.” It was narrated by Muhammad bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha"
"1532","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb told us, my uncle told me, Haywa told me, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Sulayman, in the same way, and he said: She said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “And he pardoned the muezzin.” Abu Bakr said: Al-A’mash has a better memorization than two hundred people, like Muhammad bin Abi Salih."
